Hi,

I think what happened is that you did not install the packages using:

source("http://www.braju.com/R/hbLite.R")
hbInstall("aroma.affymetrix")

but by other means - is that correct?  Did you go to r-forge? If so,
do *not* do that, because that is code under development that you
should never use.  Always use the above approach.

The problem is that you picked up aroma.core v1.2.1 and R.filesets
v0.6.0 which aroma.affymetrix v1.2.0 is not compatible with.

To solve this, a workaround is to reinstall aroma.core and R.filesets
from CRAN(!):

install.packages("R.filesets")
install.packages("aroma.core")

Does this solve your problem?

/Henrik

